

This patch helps the noce_try_cond_arith look through a copy insn
which makes that block not simple, given that the else was simple
in the first place. Only a single copy insn is looked through here
so the insn where the copy's value is defined is the first insn in
that block ignoring the note and debug insns. SET_SRC gets to the
definition if all the conditions are satisfied and successfully
looks through the copy.

This patch relies on the liveness check on bb_valid_for_noce_process_p.
I also included the PATTERN check so as to not drop a clobber along with
the check that original destination is a register so that it cannot hold
a reference to the dropped if_info->a.

Bootstrapped and regtested in x86_64-pc-linux-gnu with no new fails
except for gcc.target/i386/shift-gf2p8affine-2.c.It fails with SIGILL
on my test machine, which lacks AVX512 (my earlier baseline was from
a machine that had it), and it fails the same way without the patch.
and I also ran the riscv.exp (compile tests) with -march=rv64gcb_zicond
-mabi=lp64d and noticed no new fails.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	PR rtl-optimization/122335
	* ifcvt.cc (noce_try_cond_arith): Made the function look through a copy insn given the conditions passed.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	PR rtl-optimization/122335
	* gcc.target/riscv/pr122335-1.c : New Test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/pr122335-2.c : New Test which failed on v1.

Signed-off-by: Souradipto Das <souradiptodas6@gmail.com>
